        "timestamp": 1792771909
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14962#discussion_r4361650889\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, it exists to just make sure that we also compile the non-owner code path, but we can't really actually run it in the wast tests without host cooperation. Maybe it makes more sense as a disas test? Or do you think it is worth promoting to a <code>#[test]</code> and actually running the code?</p>\n</blockquote>",
